### ===== AUTH =====

### Sign up → 201 (returns a token)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Roy",
  "email": "roy@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

### Sign up with the same email → 409
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Roy again",
  "email": "ROY@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

### Sign up with a short password → 400
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sara",
  "email": "sara@example.com",
  "password": "123"
}

### Sign up with a bad email and no name → 400
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

### Log in → 200 (copy the token into @token above)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "roy@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

### Log in with the wrong password → 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "roy@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Log in with an unknown email → 401 (same message)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

### Who am I → 200
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Who am I without a token → 401
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### Who am I with a fake token → 401
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi


### ===== ITEMS =====

### Create an item → 201 (copy its _id into @itemId above)
POST {{host}}/api/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "found",
  "title": "Black wallet",
  "category": "cards-ids",
  "location": "Library",
  "date": "2026-11-08"
}

### Create without a token → 401
POST {{host}}/api/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "found",
  "title": "Black wallet",
  "category": "cards-ids",
  "location": "Library",
  "date": "2026-11-08"
}

### Create with bad data → 400
POST {{host}}/api/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "stolen",
  "title": "",
  "category": "food",
  "date": "banana"
}

### Create with malformed JSON → 400
POST {{host}}/api/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "broken json",

### List all items → 200 (public, no token needed)
GET {{host}}/api/items

### Get one item → 200 (public)
GET {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}

### Get with an invalid id → 400
GET {{host}}/api/items/banana

### Get an id that doesn't exist → 404
GET {{host}}/api/items/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011

### Update one field with PATCH → 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "Cafeteria"
}

### Update with PUT → 200
PUT {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Brown leather wallet"
}

### Update without a token → 401
PATCH {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Not logged in"
}

### Update with invalid data → 400
PATCH {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": ""
}

### Update with no allowed fields → 400
PATCH {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "closed"
}

### Update an id that doesn't exist → 404
PATCH {{host}}/api/items/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Nothing here"
}

### A second user signs up → 201 (copy her token into @otherToken)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sara",
  "email": "sara@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

### Sara tries to edit Roy's item → 403
PATCH {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mine now"
}

### Sara tries to delete Roy's item → 403
DELETE {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### Roy can still edit his own item → 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Black wallet (still mine)"
}

### Delete without a token → 401
DELETE {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}

### Delete → 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete the same item again → 404
DELETE {{host}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete with an invalid id → 400
DELETE {{host}}/api/items/banana
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ===== OTHER =====

### Unknown route → 404
GET {{host}}/api/pizza